sed tier; battery on deck) — 8 mm spare,1520.98,171.0,1691.98,True,True,False\n4,33.61,58.4,AF3a,iFlight Chimera9 ECO,Lumenier NAV 12000mAh 6S 21700 Amprius,6,1750.7,14.9,PurpleRiver Mini 640 (T13),NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (SBC3),Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (DVR9),included with airframe,included with airframe,included with airframe,GEPRC ELRS Nano 2.4G PA100 (GEPRCNanoPA100),CVBS,Skydroid 150CH 5.8GHz True-Diversity UVC Receiver,fits,110x70,90x62,top,fits (SBC on a raised tier; battery on deck) — 8 mm spare,1567.47,171.0,1738.47,True,True,False\n5,30.74,48.2,AF4a,DarwinFPV X9,Upgrade Energy GREEN V2 6S2P 8Ah Amprius SA10,6,1469.7,11.3,PurpleRiver Mini 640 (T13),NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (SBC3),Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (DVR9),included with airframe,included with airframe,TBS M10 GPS (G6),GEPRC ELRS Nano 2.4G PA100 (GEPRCNanoPA100),CVBS,Skydroid 150CH 5.8GHz True-Diversity UVC Receiver,marginal,100x60,90x62,top,\"marginal: SBC 90x62 vs deck 100x60 mm (-2 mm) — snug/custom deck, slight overhang\",1397.98,171.0,1568.98,True,True,False\n6,30.55,49.2,AF3a,iFlight Chimera9 ECO,Upgrade Energy GREEN V2 6S2P 8Ah Amprius SA10,6,1447.7,12.3,PurpleRiver Mini 640 (T13),NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (SBC3),Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (DVR9),included with airframe,included with airframe,included with airframe,GEPRC ELRS Nano 2.4G PA100 (GEPRCNanoPA100),CVBS,Skydroid 150CH 5.8GHz True-Diversity UVC Receiver,fits,110x70,90x62,top,fits (SBC on a raised tier; battery on deck) — 8 mm spare,1439.98,171.0,1610.98,True,True,False\n7,30.42,45.2,AF4a,DarwinFPV X9,GNB (Gaoneng) 6S3P 12Ah 21700 Li-ion,6,2102.7,16.2,PurpleRiver Mini 640 (T13),NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (SBC3),Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (DVR9),included with airframe,included with airframe,TBS M10 GPS (G6),GEPRC ELRS Nano 2.4G PA100 (GEPRCNanoPA100),CVBS,Skydroid 150CH 5.8GHz True-Diversity UVC Receiver,marginal,100x60,90x62,top,\"marginal: SBC 90x62 vs deck 100x60 mm (-2 mm) — snug/custom deck, slight overhang\",1313.98,171.0,1484.98,True,True,False\n8,30.07,45.9,AF4a,DarwinFPV X9,Lumenier NAV 10000mAh 6S 21700 Li-Ion,6,1827.7,14.1,PurpleRiver Mini 640 (T13),NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (SBC3),Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (DVR9),included with airframe,included with airframe,TBS M10 GPS (G6),GEPRC ELRS Nano 2.4G PA100 (GEPRCNanoPA100),CVBS,Skydroid 150CH 5.8GHz True-Diversity UVC Receiver,marginal,100x60,90x62,top,\"marginal: SBC 90x62 vs deck 100x60 mm (-2 mm) — snug/custom deck, slight overhang\",1353.97,171.0,1524.97,True,True,False\n9,30.03,45.8,AF3a,iFlight Chimera9 ECO,GNB (Gaoneng) 6S3P 12Ah 21700 Li-ion,6,2080.7,17.7,PurpleRiver Mini 640 (T13),NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (SBC3),Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (DVR9),included with airframe,included with airframe,included with airframe,GEPRC ELRS Nano 2.4G PA100 (GEPRCNanoPA100),CVBS,Skydroid 150CH 5.8GHz True-Diversity UVC Receiver,fits,110x70,90x62,top,fits (SBC on a raised tier; battery on deck) — 8 mm spare,1355.98,171.0,1526.98,True,True,False\n\n[26 more lines in file. Use offset=11 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1783025695912}}
{"type":"message","id":"150b92b1","parentId":"19e2f02b","timestamp":"2026-07-02T20:54:55.913Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_a026e82813df4615b5068299","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# System Engineering Plan\n\nThe build proceeds in **three incremental phases** (merged from the original four —\nthe old Phase 1 \"basic flight\" and Phase 2 \"FPV + waypoints\" are now a single Phase 1).\nSelected parts: [`SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md`](SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md); full phased bill of\nmaterials: [`BOM.md`](BOM.md).\n\n## Phase 1 — Basic Flight + FPV Downlink + Waypoints\n**Goal** — Stable manual line-of-sight flight, live analog video on the laptop, and\npre-programmed waypoint missions.\n\n**Requirements**\n- R4_AF_PAYLOAD, R4_AF_WT, R4_AF_ASSY, R4_AF_STIFF, R4_AF_LANDING, R4_AF_COST, R4_AF_PROP_CFG, R4_AF_PWR_DIST\n- R4_BAT_VOLT, R4_BAT_WT, R4_BAT_IF\n- R4_GCS_VIDEO_DISP, R4_GCS_RANGE, R4_GCS_IF, R4_GCS_CTRL, R4_GCS_TELEM\n\n**Components Required**\n- Airframe — **iFlight Chimera9 ECO 9\" PNP** (`AF3a`); bundles a 5.8 GHz analog VTX + FPV camera (air-side video, $0)\n- RadioReceiver — **iFlight True Diversity ELRS** (`iFlightTD`); RC control + telemetry on one link\n- Battery — **Upgrade Energy GREEN V2 6S3P 12 Ah Amprius** (`BAT10`, flight default) + **2× GNB 6S3P 12 Ah** (`BAT22`, development packs)\n- RadioControlTransmitter — **RadioMaster Boxer ELRS** (`TX1`, handheld)\n- ELRS USB dongle — primary laptop control + telemetry link (TBD)\n- GPS — **TBS M10** (`G6`) for waypoint navigation\n- VideoReceiver — **Skydroid 150CH 5.8 GHz UVC** (`VRX6`); laptop-direct video\n- Antenna — **TrueRC X-AIR 5.8 patch** (`PATCH1`); video-link range margin (see `analysis/rf_link_budget.md`)\n- Anti-spark filter — **iFlight Anti Spark** (`ASF1`, XT60 inline)\n- Battery charger — **HOTA D6 Pro** (`CHG1`, 6S Li-ion/LiPo, bench/reusable)\n- GCS laptop (MacBook — existing equipment, $0)\n\n**Phase Steps**\n\n[52 more lines in file. Use offset=31 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1783025695913}}
{"type":"message","id":"b5917550","parentId":"150b92b1","timestamp":"2026-07-02T20:54:55.914Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6cae0beb1cc84b068a7e965c","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"package DroneCandidates {\n doc /*\n  * Candidate option library for the Surveillance Drone.\n  *\n  * Single source of truth for the component market/trade-study data that used to\n  * live in analysis/*.csv. Each candidate is a SysML v2 part usage typed by the\n  * matching definition in DroneSystemModel::Architecture, with attribute values\n  * bound via redefinition (:>>). This keeps the option data co-located with the\n  * model schema it conforms to.\n  *\n  * Conventions:\n  *  - Usage name carries the CSV row ID (airframes prefixed \"AF\" since SysML\n  *    names cannot start with a digit). Original model name is in `name`.\n  *  - Cost ranges are bound to a single representative value; the range is noted\n  *    in a trailing comment.\n  *  - Sub-units absent from the SI library (mW, mA, mK, um) are bound in base SI\n  *    units with the original value in a comment: 100 mW -> 0.1 [W],\n  *    120 mA -> 0.12 [A], 50 mK -> 0.05 [K], 12 um -> 0.012 [mm].\n  *  - Attributes with only \"Unknown\"/\"N/A\"/estimate-only CSV data are omitted and\n  *    recorded in MODEL_ISSUES.md.\n  *  - Derived analysis columns (Johnson criteria, GSD, NPU load margin, pass/fail)\n  *    are NOT component attributes and are intentionally excluded — they belong to\n  *    the Analysis layer.\n  */\n\n private import ScalarValues::*;\n private import SI::*;\n private import DroneSystemModel::Architecture::*;  // the component part definitions\n\n // =========================================================================\n // AIRFRAME CANDIDATES  (source: analysis/airframe-candidates.csv)\n // =========================================================================\n package AirframeCandidates {\n\n  // NOTE: GEPRC MARK4 LR7 (formerly AF1) REMOVED 2026-06-27 — discontinued.\n  // Replaced with the current GEPRC MOZ7 V2 family (Analog / WTFPV / O4 Pro),\n  // which share one platform: 336mm, 7.5in HQ props, SPEEDX2 2809 1280KV motors,\n  // TAKER H743 BT FC, TAKER H65 8S 65A ESC, GEP-M1025 GPS, 6S LiPo / 8S Li-ion.\n\n  part AF1a : Airframe {\n   :>> minCells_s = 6;  // 6S LiPo / 8S Li-ion capable (H65 8S ESC, 2809 1280KV)\n   :>> maxCells_s = 8;\n   :>> maxThrustPerMotor_g = 3000.0;  // EST: SPEEDX2 2809 1280KV on 7.5in @6S (GEPRC publishes no grams)\n   :>> name = \"GEPRC MOZ7 V2 Analog\";\n   :>> purchaseUrl = \"https://geprc.com/product/geprc-moz7-v2-analog-long-range-fpv-drone/\";\n   :>> purchaseType = \"PNP\";\n   :>> cost_USD = 459.99;            // 459.99-501.99 (PNP -> ELRS/TBS BNF)\n   :>> mass = 782.0 [g];            // confirmed: GEPRC \"782g +/-10g without battery\" (incl analog VTX + cam + GPS)\n   :>> propSize_in = 7.5;\n   :>> wheelbase = 336.0 [mm];\n\n[3827 more lines in file. Use offset=51 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1783025695913}}
{"type":"message","id":"815e5c21","parentId":"b5917550","timestamp":"2026-07-02T20:55:02.113Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"David asked me to git pull and inventory all the extensive changes. I've now read through all the major new/modified files. Let me give him a comprehensive summary of what changed.\n\nLet me also check a few more things — the CLAUDE.md (renamed from the original), README.md, and the model.sysml changes.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_14b600fdb562449e9049d69b","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/CLAUDE.md","limit":40},"partialArgs":"{\"path\": \"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/CLAUDE.md\", \"limit\": 40}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_a486a1b1285e403d9d9a15ca","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md","limit":40},"partialArgs":"{\"path\": \"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md\", \"limit\": 40}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":48708,"output":220,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":69,"totalTokens":48928,"cost":{"input":0.0048708,"output":0.000044,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0049147999999999996}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1783025695917,"responseId":"gen-1783025696-PvyjVpYikAdAWzzfzIe4"}}
{"type":"message","id":"0f467b52","parentId":"815e5c21","timestamp":"2026-07-02T20:55:02.167Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_14b600fdb562449e9049d69b","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# CLAUDE.md\n\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\n\n## What this repository is\n\nThis is a **Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE)** project for a thermal surveillance drone (wildlife scouting), not a software codebase. There is no build, lint, or test toolchain — the \"source\" is engineering documentation: a SysML v2 textual model plus trade studies that evaluate real, commercially-available components against it. The work follows Agile MBSE with **git as the source of truth** for engineering decisions.\n\n> **Currently selected components — read [`SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md`](SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md) first.** It is the single authoritative list of what is LOCKED vs OPEN (airframe, thermal camera, SBC, …). Locks are machine-enforced by the `FIXED_*` constants in [`analysis/flight_time_model.py`](analysis/flight_time_model.py); rationale is logged in `MODEL_ISSUES.md`. Keep `SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md` in sync whenever a selection changes.\n\n## SysML v2 authoring (tooling + syntax reference)\n\nBefore editing the model, lean on the installed tooling and the syntax reference:\n\n- **Extension:** Syside Editor (`sensmetry.syside-editor`) is installed and gives live validation, completion, hover, and navigation for SysML v2 (language id `sysml`, free, no Java). The model targets **SysML v2.0 Beta 4**.\n- **Syntax reference:** [`reference/sysml-v2-syntax.md`](reference/sysml-v2-syntax.md) is a project-tailored cheat sheet (def/usage, ports/connections, `subsets`/`satisfy` traceability, constraints/analysis, `:>`/`:>>`/`::>` operators). [`reference/sysml-v2-cheatsheet-examples.sysml`](reference/sysml-v2-cheatsheet-examples.sysml) is the canonical, extension-validated example of every construct — open it to confirm exact syntax.\n- **The model files are `model.sysml` (schema) and [`candidates.sysml`](candidates.sysml) (data).** `model.sysml` holds requirements, the component `part def`s, and analysis. `candidates.sysml` holds the ~110 real component options (migrated from `analysis/*.csv`) as typed part usages with `:>>` value bindings — the single source of truth for market/trade-study data. It imports the defs via `DroneSystemModel::Architecture::*`.\n- **Validation:** both files currently parse cleanly under Syside. `model.sysml` imports `ScalarValues`, `SI`, and (in `Architecture`) `Requirements::**` so primitives, units, and `satisfy` refs resolve. Keep it that way — run \"Restart language server\" if diagnostics look stale.\n- **Trust the live diagnostics when editing** — the original model had several latent SysML v2 errors that only surfaced once the LSP was applied (see [`MODEL_ISSUES.md`](MODEL_ISSUES.md)). Don't assume a construct is valid because it \"looks right\"; the editor will tell you.\n\nThe hard design constraints driving everything: **≤ $2,500 total system cost**, **≥ 30 min flight time** (60 min stretch), **2.8 km range**, thermal detection/classification of deer/turkey/humans at 90–120 m AGL, and minimizing DIY soldering.\n\n## Critical rule: do not modify `model.sysml` without approval\n\n`model.sysml` is the authoritative system model and a protected artifact. **Never modify, move, or delete it without explicit prior approval from the user (David).** Changes require documented justification and a clear git commit. This is a standing policy — treat edits to `model.sysml` as requiring a formal request first, even for changes that look trivial.\n\n## The system model (`model.sysml`)\n\nA single SysML v2 textual file, one top-level `package DroneSystemModel` containing four sub-packages. Understanding how they interlock is the key to being productive here:\n\n- **Requirements** — Top-level mission requirements `R1`–`R8` (note: `R3_1`/`R3_2`, not `R3.1`/`R3.2` — dots are invalid identifiers), plus per-subsystem requirement packages (`CameraRequirements`, `BatterySubsystem`, `SBCSubsystem`, `GCSSubsystem`, `AirframeSubsystem`). Subsystem requirements use `subsets` to trace up to the mission requirement they decompose (e.g. `R3_CAM_FOV subsets R3`, cost requirements `subsets R4`). Requirement IDs follow `R<n>_<SUBSYS>_<NAME>` (e.g. `R4_AF_PAYLOAD`). (The requirements package is `CameraRequirements`, deliberately distinct from the `CameraSubsystem` *part def* to avoid a name collision.)\n- **Architecture** — `part def`s for each component (`Airframe`, `Battery`, `CameraSubsystem`, `FpvCamera`, `GpsModule`, `SingleBoardComputerPayload`, `RadioReceiver`, `VideoTransmitter`, `ThermalVideoRecorder`, `VideoReceiver`, `UsbVideoCapture`, etc.). Each part carries `attribute`s (cost_USD, mass, power…), `port`s, and formal `satisfy` statements linking it back to the requirements it fulfills. `SurveillanceDrone` composes the airborne parts and wires them with `interface connect`; `AerialThermalObservationSystem` composes drone + `GroundControlStation` + `ViewingComputer` and connects the wireless RF links. Derived attributes (`totalPower`, `totalCost`, `subTotalCost`) roll up from the leaf parts. A **`Compatibility`** sub-package (added 2026-06-26) declares which component pairings form a *real* configuration as formal SysML v2 — typed `port def`s, `enum def`s (`VideoFormat`, `RfBand`), `constraint def`s, and `interface def`s for the battery↔airframe cell-count rule (P1), the video-format chain (V1–V4), and RF band (R1–R2). `Airframe` carries `minCells_s`/`maxCells_s` for the voltage rule. The component part defs' power/video/RF ports are **typed** to these port defs, and the battery-power + video connects in `SurveillanceDrone` are typed to their interface defs (data/GNSS ports stay untyped). Syside validates the structure; the **rules are enforced by the flight-time sweep** (`model.sysml` declares, `flight_time_model.py` executes — see §C11-C12 in [`MODEL_ISSUES.md`](MODEL_ISSUES.md)).\n- **Analysis** — A full parametric verification layer: `calc def`s `FlightTimeCalc` (energy / power → flight time, typed `ScalarQuantityValue` since ISQ `/` doesn't narrow to `DurationValue`) and `ScoreCalc` (flight-time magnitude / cost, via `QuantityCalculations::ToReal`); `constraint def`s `BudgetLimit` (R4, ≤ $2,500), `MinFlightTimeReq` (R6, ≥ 1800 s), `StretchFlightTimeReq` (R8, ≥ 3600 s); and two `analysis def` cases — `MinFlightTimeCheck` (subject = system; `assert constraint` on R4 + R6, returns a boolean verdict) and `TradeSpaceEvaluation` (subject = candidate; computes score + asserts budget). Thermal detection is also modeled (B3): `calc def`s `GroundSampleDistance`/`PixelsAcrossTarget`, `constraint def`s `DetectionCriterion` (≥1.5 px)/`RecognitionCriterion` (≥4 px), and `analysis def`s `ThermalDetectionCheck` (120 m, R3_1) / `ThermalRecognitionCheck` (90 m, R3_2/R3_CAM_RES) — Johnson-criteria pixels-on-target. Requirement checks compare dimensionally (`flightTime >= 1800 [s]`). Battery energy must be in joules `[J]` (`Wh × 3600`). Syside validates structure but does not execute the calcs — numeric verdicts need a SysML v2 execution engine (see [`MODEL_ISSUES.md`](MODEL_ISSUES.md) §A10).\n- **Views** (added 2026-06-27) — Four SysML v2 `view def` + `view` presentations that `expose` model slices by stakeholder concern: `operationalMission` (mission requirements + system context), `logicalArchitecture` (system/drone/GCS decomposition), `interfaceBehavior` (the `Compatibility` interface layer + connections), and `systemVerification` (the Analysis layer). Syside validates the structure; diagram/table rendering needs a SysML v2 viewer. **Gotcha:** `verification` (like `interface`, `view`, `analysis`) is a reserved keyword, so the usage is named `systemVerification`, not `verification`.\n\nWhen editing the model (after approval), preserve the traceability web: a new requirement should `subsets` its parent, and a new/changed part should `satisfy` the requirements it covers and feed the derived cost/power rollups. To add a component **option**, add a typed usage to the matching package in `candidates.sysml` (e.g. `part X : Airframe { :>> cost_USD = …; … }`) rather than editing the def.\n\nNote on the `power` port: the seven payload part defs name their power input port `power_in` (not `power`, which would collide with the `attribute power` rollup). New connects should use `…power_in`.\n\nNote: `ViewingComputer` is an existing MacBook Air — modeled as an external actor and **excluded from `totalCost`** because it is not procured. Components bundled with an airframe carry `includedWithAirframe : Boolean` and are costed as $0 in budget buildups.\n\n[52 more lines in file. Use offset=41 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1783025702167}}
{"type":"message","id":"bb24279f","parentId":"0f467b52","timestamp":"2026-07-02T20:55:02.168Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_a486a1b1285e403d9d9a15ca","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Thermal Surveillance Drone — MBSE Project\n\nA **Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE)** project to architect, select, and build a\nthermal surveillance drone for personal wildlife scouting. The \"source\" is engineering\ndocumentation — a **SysML v2** textual model plus trade studies that evaluate real,\ncommercially-available components against it — with **git as the source of truth** for\nengineering decisions. There is no build/lint/test toolchain.\n\n## Mission & hard constraints\n\nDetect and classify **deer, turkey, and humans** thermally at **90–120 m AGL**, subject to:\n\n| Constraint | Target |\n|---|---|\n| Total system cost (R4) | **≤ $2,500** |\n| Flight time (R6 / R8 stretch) | **≥ 30 min** (60 min stretch) |\n| Range — control **and** video (R7 / R4_GCS_RANGE) | **≥ 2.8 km** (hard, both links) |\n| Thermal detect / recognize (R3) | Johnson ≥1.5 px @120 m / ≥4 px @90 m |\n| Build | minimize DIY soldering; laptop is the ground station |\n\n## Current status\n\nPast the early design phase — requirements, logical architecture, a full parametric\nverification layer, and **extensive component trade studies** are complete. Components\nare now being **locked in**:\n\n- ✅ **Airframe — iFlight Chimera9 ECO (9\")** · ✅ **Thermal — PurpleRiver Mini 640 (640×512, USB)** · ✅ **SBC — NanoPi M5 (RK3576)**\n- 🔶 Open: PNP-vs-BNF variant, battery (6S 12 Ah Amprius — Lumenier vs Upgrade Energy), GPS, RX, DVR, and ground-station specifics.\n- **Reference build:** Chimera9 ECO + Lumenier 6S 12 Ah Amprius + Mini 640 + NanoPi M5 → **~58.6 min hover, ~$1,645 system** (well under the $2,500 cap).\n\n> **The authoritative, current list of selected vs open components is [`SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md`](SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md).** Read it first.\n\nNext up: **physical integration** — designing a 3D-printed deck to mount the SBC + thermal\ncamera on the airframe (see [`reference/cad-resources.md`](reference/cad-resources.md)).\n\n## Repository layout\n\n| Path | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| [`model.sysml`](model.sysml) | Authoritative SysML v2 system model — requirements, component `part def`s, compatibility, analysis, views. **Protected** (changes need explicit approval). |\n\n[78 more lines in file. Use offset=41 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1783025702168}}
{"type":"message","id":"09ca95ab","parentId":"bb24279f","timestamp":"2026-07-02T20:55:30.435Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Okay, David asked me to pull the repo and take inventory of all the extensive changes. I've now read through all the major new/changed files. Let me compile a comprehensive summary.\n\nThe git log shows 23 files changed with 3,701 insertions and 4,160 deletions. Let me break this down into what's new vs what's been modified.\n\n**New files:**\n1. `BOM.md` - Bill of Materials, phased procurement list\n2. `SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md` - Single source of truth for locked/open component selections\n3. `MODEL_ISSUES.md` - Issues log with decisions, defects, open items\n4. `REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md` - Formal SSS (DI-IPSC-81431)\n5. `INTERFACE_REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md` - Formal IRS (DI-IPSC-81434)\n6. `analysis/rf_link_budget.md` - RF link budget analysis\n7. `analysis/rf_link_budget.py` - Python script that generates the RF link budget\n8. `analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.csv` - CSV export of top value configs\n9. `analysis/openhd-air-wifi-adapter-trade-study.md` - OpenHD air-side WiFi adapter study\n10. `analysis/openhd-ground-antenna-trade-study.md` - OpenHD ground antenna trade study\n11. `analysis/openhd-ground-wifi-adapter-trade-study.md` - OpenHD ground-side WiFi adapter study\n12. `reference/cad-resources.md` - CAD resources for physical integration\n\nLet me compile a concise summary for David.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"text","text":"Here's the full inventory of changes since the last pull. Quite a bit of work went in:\n\n---\n\n## 🆕 New Files (12 created)\n\n### Architecture / Requirements (formal docs)\n- **`BOM.md`** — Full phased Bill of Materials. 3 phases, total ~$2,360 all-in (~$2,028 per-drone R4 cost). Phase 1 = $1,355 (flight + FPV + waypoints), Phase 2 = ~$864 (thermal + DVR + OpenHD), Phase 3 = $141 (SBC autonomy).\n- **`SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md`** — Single authoritative source of truth for ✅ locked vs 🔶 open selections. 15 components locked, including: airframe (Chimera9 ECO PNP), RX (iFlight True Diversity ELRS), radio (RadioMaster TX12 MkII), VRX (Skydroid 150CH UVC), antenna (TrueRC X-AIR patch), battery flight (Upgrade Energy 6S 12Ah Amprius), dev batteries (GNB ×2), GPS (BLITZ M10 bundled), charger (HOTA D6 Pro), ELRS dongle (HGLRC Hermes), SBC (NanoPi M5), thermal (PurpleRiver Mini 640), OpenHD air (LB-LINK BL-M8812EU2), OpenHD ground (Alfa AWUS036ACH), OpenHD ground antennas (Foxeer Echo 2 Max ×2). Includes locked/enforced-in-analysis notes, rationale links to MODEL_ISSUES.\n- **`MODEL_ISSUES.md`** — Comprehensive issues/decisions log. 19 model defects fixed (A1–A8), 22 decisions/resolutions (B1–D), open items tracked with status. **This is the project's institutional memory** — everything from `refines`→`subsets` fix, KOLAS7 mass corrections, GEPRC MARK4→MOZ7 replacement, DVR staging, physical fit checks, RF link budget, phase restructure, and more.\n- **`REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md`** — Formal System/Subsystem Specification (SSS) aligned to DI-IPSC-81431. Exports all requirements from `model.sysml` with verification methods and traceability.\n- **`INTERFACE_REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md`** — Formal Interface Requirements Specification (IRS) aligned to DI-IPSC-81434. All interfaces with compatibility rules (P1 battery voltage, V video format, R RF band).\n\n### Analysis / Trade Studies\n- **`analysis/rf_link_budget.py`** — Python script computing FSPL + fade margin for every RF link at 2.8 km. Generates the markdown report.\n- **`analysis/rf_link_budget.md`** — Results: **All links PASS with 10 dB margin**. Video (analog + patch) = +15.3 dB, Control (ELRS 250 mW) = +23 dB, Telemetry = +19 dB, OpenHD = +11.3 dB with Foxeer Echo 2 Max pair. Also includes ground antenna options table (AXII Quadro vs Echo 2 Max vs Echo 2).\n- **`analysis/openhd-air-wifi-adapter-trade-study.md`** — 4 candidates (plus 3 eliminated). **Won: LB-LINK BL-M8812EU2** ($12, ~18g, >29 dBm, RTL8812EU, WFB-ng author's own test hardware).\n- **`analysis/openhd-ground-antenna-trade-study.md`** — 4 directional panel candidates. **Won: Foxeer Echo 2 Max** (13 dBi, 60° beam, Linear, $30/ea, RP-SMA → mates directly to AWUS036ACH). Justifies the selection vs Lumenier AXII Quadro (narrower beam, $32.49 but needs pigtails/adapters).\n- **`analysis/openhd-ground-wifi-adapter-trade-study.md`** — Candidates for ground-side USB WiFi. **Won: Alfa AWUS036ACH** (RTL8812AU, USB-C, dual RP-SMA, $65). Includes critical VM compatibility analysis: VMware Fusion xHCI, NOT UTM.\n- **`analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.csv`** — Top configs by endurance-per-dollar.\n- **`reference/cad-resources.md`** — CAD tool recommendations (FreeCAD 1.0 primary), per-component 3D model sources (or lack thereof) for Chimera9 ECO, NanoPi M5, PurpleRiver Mini 640, and battery integration. Community model links for Chimera frame family.\n\n---\n\n## 🔁 Modified Files (11 changed)\n\n### Model\n- **`model.sysml`** — Significant additions: `Antenna` part def, `Charger` part def, `AntiSparkFilter` part def, `BatteryPowerInterface` with `ConnectorCompatible` constraint, `connector` attribute on power ports, `Airframe.batteryConnector`, and refined `power_in` port naming. Updated doc comments for 3-phase plan.\n- **`candidates.sysml`** — Massive expansion (+616 lines). New candidates: PATCH1 (TrueRC X-AIR antenna), CHG1–CHG4 (chargers), ASF1 (anti-spark filter), VRX6/VRX7 (better ground receivers), VRX8/VRX9 (DJI/Walksnail digital goggles), WLAN_AIR1 (OpenHD air), WLAN_GND1 (OpenHD ground), ANT_GND1/ANT_GND2 (Foxeer antennas). Updated: G4 GPS pre-installed on AF3a, BAT10 is now flight default (BAT09 OOS), BAT22 dev packs added. Airframe masses refined (AF3a now 729g with GPS).\n\n### Analysis / Flight-Time\n- **`analysis/flight_time_model.py`** — Major rewrite (+320 lines). Now: reads real battery candidates from `candidates.sysml`; 3-phase-aware cost buildup with locked airframe enforced; GCS cost = $126 base (radio + dongle + patch) plus per-config matched VRX by video format; OpenHD WLAN components added to cost; charger/anti-spark folded in; physical fit check (3-tier: fits/marginal/no_fit) with deck dimension parsing; battery connector check; battery mount position (top/bottom).\n- **`analysis/flight_time_results.csv`** — ~387 lines of new config results with locked-airframe-only sweep.\n- **`analysis/flight_time_results.md`** — Updated summary with locked Chimera9 ECO focus.\n- **`analysis/flight_time_instances.sysml`** — Regenerated with locked-airframe instances (much smaller file, -3,714 lines).\n- **`analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.md`** — Top 34 now ranked. #1: DarwinFPV X9 + Upgrade Energy 6S 12Ah = 33.89 min/$1k, 55.9 min hover, $1,650 system. #3: Chimera9 ECO + same battery = 33.62 min/$1k, 56.9 min, $1,692. Both fit R4 well under cap.\n- **`analysis/cost_vs_flighttime.png`** — Updated scatter plot.\n\n### Documentation\n- **`CLAUDE.md`** — Now points first to `SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md`, adds guidance for `candidates.sysml` as data source, notes protected-model rule, documents new model constructs (Compatibility, Analysis, Views packages), and references new artifacts.\n- **`README.md`** — Updated status (airframe locked ✅, components locking, open items), new repo layout listing all new files with descriptions, refined architecture section, points to SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md as authoritative.\n- **`systems_engineering_plan.md`** — Restructured from 4 phases → 3 phases: Phase 1 = merged basic flight + FPV + waypoints (was Phase 1+2), Phase 2 = thermal + DVR + OpenHD (was Phase 3), Phase 3 = SBC autonomy (was Phase 4). GPS and ELRS dongle pulled into Phase 1. Updated component lists and test milestones.\n\n---\n\n**Bottom line:** The project has transitioned from early design/trade studies into a detailed build plan with locked components, formal SSS/IRS export docs, a full RF link budget, a costed phased BOM, OpenHD studies for all three links (air adapter, ground adapter, ground antennas), and CAD resources for the physical integration phase. The Chimera9 ECO is locked, the ~$2,360 BOM fits under the $2,500 cap with ~$140 headroom, and everything's documented with traceability back to the model."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":10800,"output":2280,"cacheRead":40960,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":357,"totalTokens":54040,"cost":{"input":0.00108,"output":0.00045599999999999997,"cacheRead":0.0008192,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0023552}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1783025702178,"responseId":"gen-1783025702-8cbszNyR3hBiBRgNEiw6"}}
